{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/122779-worm-more-aberrant-inspiration","id":122779,"title":"Worm-More Aberrant Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-30T16:58:59-07:00","id":122779,"title":"Worm-More Aberrant Inspiration","content":"So I just got done reading <a href=\"http://parahumans.wordpress.com/table-of-contents/\" target=\"_blank\">Worm</a>. Reading this web serial made me want to run Aberrant harder than anything has ever made me want to run any game. Lots of smart, interesting characters, lots of supervillain/superhero tropes examined, lots of people using weird or weak powers in clever ways, lots of Team Tomorrow inspiration with the good guys' PR machine.<br /> <br /> Those of you running or making Aberrant? This here is an inspirational gold mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T17:26:48-07:00","id":122788,"title":"","content":"Atomic Robo is also excellent inspiration (or, should I say, Inspiration) for an Adventure! game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T12:41:04-07:00","id":125301,"title":"","content":"The comic book Tom Strong is great for Adventure! inspiration. Also, you should peruse Planetary when you want some great ideas to use for Adventure! or Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 05-05-2014, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T14:52:11-07:00","id":126158,"title":"","content":"Comic books that inspire me for Aberrant<br /> <br /> New Avengers and Avengers (Hickman's runs)<br /> Supergod<br /> Uber<br /> Supreme Power (Straczynski's run, though it was cut short because he never finishes anything, was very good at providing an insight into superhuman psychology)<br /> Ultimates (all of it. I don't like Millar's run in the particulars, but the tone of the world works very well for it. Hickman and Humphries nail it though)<br /> Planetary<br /> The Authority<br /> Uncanny X-Men (Gillen's run with the Extinction Squad)<br /> Iron Man: Extremis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T23:22:35-07:00","id":128026,"title":"","content":"I pretty much lost interest in the mainline comics as they sunk into the iron age, and stopped reading them entirely about the time they hit rust so a lot of my inspiration comes from old bronze age comics I have or some of the newer movies like the Avengers and its tie-ins. Some science fiction works too if it features high powered psi or tech &quot;powers&quot; that can be adapted to Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T07:17:11-07:00","id":150300,"title":"","content":"Right now my main inspiration for Aberrant games is the webcomic <a href=\"http://strongfemaleprotagonist.com/issue-1/page-0/\" target=\"_blank\">Strong Female Protagonist</a>. I swear it's like the writer was an Aberrant player at one point, because it hits everything right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T15:49:46-07:00","id":150861,"title":"","content":"Wow I\u00b4m loving worm but I have to say that the webcomic you linked Aiden is fantastic! I'm having a blast with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:09:16-07:00","id":152759,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Strong Female Protagonist makes me happy. Just backed the Kickstarter for the book on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}